# [DD-13b.W1.1 r46sem finding 20] TWO BLOCKS NAMING THEMSELVES `x`. The
# spec has always said a block's `name` is in the FILE namespace and must
# be unique within the file, but that was enforced only by pcrec, which
# tests/harness/run.sh never calls for a HEADLESS file -- i.e. every file
# in the corpus today. This file is deliberately headless (no head
# declaration at all), so it is the population every corpus file is in.
pattern a+
name x
m "aaa" 0 3

pattern b+
name x
m "bbb" 0 3
